DS3D sensor-fusion cluster is an implementation of `ds3d::datafilter` which
clusters the per-sensor 3D detections carried in a `ds3d::datamap` into a single
fused object list, merging duplicate detections that the individual LiDAR and
camera models reported for the same physical object.

DS3D is framework agnostic. There is no gstreamer/Glib dependencies. Any framework could
simply wrap DS3D modules.

`libnvds_3d_sensor_fusion_cluster.so` is built from these source files. and the
cluster filter is created through API `CreateFilter_SensorFusionCluster`.
Application users can call this API to instantiate this datafilter.

The config content shall as:

    type: ds3d::datafilter
    out_caps: ds3d/datamap
    custom_lib_path: libnvds_3d_sensor_fusion_cluster.so
    custom_create_function: CreateFilter_SensorFusionCluster
    config_body:
       ...

Any custom `ds3d::datafilter` must derive from `ds3d::BaseImplDataFilter` for data processing
And implement the following interfaces:

    ErrCode startImpl(const std::string& content, const std::string& path) override;
    ErrCode processImpl(
        GuardDataMap datamap, OnGuardDataCBImpl outputDataCb,
        OnGuardDataCBImpl inputConsumedCb) override;
    ErrCode stopImpl() override;
    ErrCode flushImpl() override;

In addition, users also need export a C-API for application to intiate this datafilter.
The exported C-API name is not limited. In this sample, it is `CreateFilter_SensorFusionCluster`.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libglm Development package (header-only matrix/vector math)
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this `ds3d::datafilter` lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_3d_sensor_fusion_cluster.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
